XeGfx builds against third-party sources that are not included in this
repository: FreeBSD's drm-kmod, FreeBSD's LinuxKPI, the Linux DRM and i915
drivers, and FreeBSD kernel headers. They are fetched separately and keep
their own licenses (drm core and i915 are mostly MIT, LinuxKPI and the
FreeBSD kernel are BSD).

shim/gen holds headers generated from FreeBSD interface (*_if.m) files with
FreeBSD's makeobjops.awk. They carry FreeBSD's BSD license.

Headers in shim/include that override FreeBSD or LinuxKPI headers are
written for XNU but may follow the shape of the files they replace; where
they copy FreeBSD code, that code keeps its BSD license and copyright.

Licences by folder
------------------

XeGfx carries every part of the Intel driver, and not all of it is under
BSD-2. Each folder keeps the licence of the code it came from:

  shim/, harness/, tools/, kext/, docs/      BSD 2-Clause (LICENSE)
  kexts/XeGfxIntelFB/                        BSD 2-Clause, written for XeGfx
  xkpi/                                      per file, see xkpi/NOTICE.md
                                             (MIT, BSD-2, PolyForm Noncommercial
                                             for the NullMoth dma-buf files)
  plugin/                                    PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
  kexts/XeGfxAccel/, kexts/XeGfxAGDC/,       PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
  kexts/NMIntelFB/
  userland/ scripts, tools, docs             BSD 2-Clause, written for XeGfx
  userland/patches/*-macos.patch             PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0,
                                             NullMoth's Darwin patches (bf2dee3)
  userland/patches/*-xegfx.patch             MIT, as Mesa and libdrm
  translator/                                LGPL-3.0 (translator/LICENSE)
  build/                                     BSD 2-Clause

plugin/, kexts/XeGfxAccel/, kexts/XeGfxAGDC/ and kexts/NMIntelFB/ are forks of
NullMoth Systems' nvidia-macos-driver
(https://github.com/nullmoth/nvidia-macos-driver), carried over from the
NvGfx fork (https://github.com/watchthelight-labs/NvGfx, branch xe-2.6.2,
commit 2b9e3b2), where their history is. The PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0
text is in licenses/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md: no commercial use, and
keep the notices. translator/ is a fork of steelbrain's metal2vulkan.

XeGfxAccel compiles against headers from NVIDIA's open-gpu-kernel-modules
(MIT, licenses/NVIDIA-open-gpu-kernel-modules-COPYING.txt), fetched
separately like drm-kmod. Mesa's licence is in licenses/Mesa-license.rst.
